<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Philip's War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1675">1675</a>–<a href="/years/1676">1676</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Metacom's War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Philip's War was fought in 1675–1676 between English colonists in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a> and Native peoples led by the Wampanoag sachem <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metacom">Metacom</a>, known to the English as King Philip. It was one of the deadliest wars of colonial American history and devastated Plymouth Colony and other settlements. Native communities suffered far heavier losses, and many survivors were killed, enslaved or driven north.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/king-philips-war.jpg" alt="King Philip's War" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: maps.bpl.org · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_map_of_New_England,_being_the_first_that_ever_was_here_cut_..._places_(2675732378).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
